  "rule": "core.metadata_brief.select_twin_partners: for each roster call in sorted order, the unused Earnings-22 call OUTSIDE the roster whose brief already measures CLOSEST to the arm's and whose ticker, country, UN region and major dialect family all DIFFER from the arm's, taking the first the symmetric padder accepts. Deterministic, injective and fixed-point-free, so no clip ever receives its own call's brief and no twin restates its arm's facts. Drawn from outside the roster because a partner inside it could state a fact that is true of another roster call; matched by the SYMMETRIC padder because a real brief can be longer than the one it twins -- the two Oceania calls render the corpus's shortest briefs and nothing that states different facts fits inside them.",
